# .bedrock/manifest — every path bedrock ships, its OWNERSHIP CLASS, and the version that added it.
# Read by scripts/update_scaffold.sh FROM THE FETCHED SOURCE (never from a child's copy, BK-09), and
# checked by scripts/check_manifest.sh (MANIFEST). One entry per line:  <path or dir/>  <class>  <since>
#
#   spine       never carries project content. Sync: identical → nothing; absent → seeded; different and
#               byte-identical to the version the project last synced from → fast-forwarded (the project
#               never touched it); different otherwise → copied to .bedrock-incoming/, NEVER overwritten.
#   seed        created once for the project to own and rewrite (0BSD, see NOTICE). Absent → seeded;
#               present → never touched.
#   project     the project's own content. Never touched by the updater.
#   maintainer  bedrock-only: removed by bootstrap, never shipped.
#   pack        opt-in: copied into a project only when selected (packs/README.md); its `files/` are seed
#               or sync per the pack's own manifest; the directory itself never ships.
# A directory entry (trailing /) classifies everything beneath it.
